    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Hello, I would like to create a comment textobject that I can use inside mini.ai\r\nI want to map this object to `q` so that `saq` select around the comment block.\r\n\r\nI know neovim added a [comment textobject here](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/f01c764cc6f82399edfa0d47a7bafbf7c95e2747/runtime/lua/vim/_comment.lua) but I don't know how to make it work with mini.ai mappings to go to next object, go to previous object, etc.\r\n\r\nAlso, I can't manage to map it to `q` because even if I map `q` to `gc`, when I type `saq` it selects around quotes, not comment.\r\n\r\nP.S Using treesitter here does not seem to work at it only select a single line of comment, not the whole block.\r\n\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hello, I would like to create a comment textobject that I can use inside mini.ai<br>\nI want to map this object to <code class=\"notranslate\">q</code> so that <code class=\"notranslate\">saq</code> select around the comment block.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I know neovim added a <a href=\"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/f01c764cc6f82399edfa0d47a7bafbf7c95e2747/runtime/lua/vim/_comment.lua\">comment textobject here</a> but I don't know how to make it work with mini.ai mappings to go to next object, go to previous object, etc.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also, I can't manage to map it to <code class=\"notranslate\">q</code> because even if I map <code class=\"notranslate\">q</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">gc</code>, when I type <code class=\"notranslate\">saq</code> it selects around quotes, not comment.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">P.S Using treesitter here does not seem to work at it only select a single line of comment, not the whole block.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Hello, I would like to create a comment textobject that I can use inside mini.ai\nI want to map this object to q so that saq select around the comment block.\nI know neovim added a comment textobject here but I don't know how to make it work with mini.ai mappings to go to next object, go to previous object, etc.\nAlso, I can't manage to map it to q because even if I map q to gc, when I type saq it selects around quotes, not comment.\nP.S Using treesitter here does not seem to work at it only select a single line of comment, not the whole block.",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
